Problem:
Define \[f(x) = (x-1)(x-3)(x-7)(x-9).\]Evaluate $f(6) - f(4)$.

Solution:
answer:  First, we need to evaluate \( f(6) \):

\[ f(6) = (6-1)(6-3)(6-7)(6-9) \]
\[ f(6) = (5)(3)(-1)(-3) \]
\[ f(6) = 15 \cdot 3 \cdot 1 \cdot (-3) \]
\[ f(6) = -45 \]

Next, we need to evaluate \( f(4) \):

\[ f(4) = (4-1)(4-3)(4-7)(4-9) \]
\[ f(4) = (3)(1)(-3)(-5) \]
\[ f(4) = 3 \cdot 1 \cdot (-3) \cdot (-5) \]
\[ f(4) = 45 \]

Now, we find \( f(6) - f(4) \):

\[ f(6) - f(4) = -45 - 45 = -90 \]

Therefore, the answer is \(\boxed{-90}\).
====================

