Problem:
A TV screen measures 24 by 16 inches. If each dimension is increased by 20$\%$, by what percent is the area increased?

Solution:
answer:  First, calculate the original area of the TV screen:
\[
\text{Original Area} = 24 \times 16 = 384 \text{ square inches}
\]

Next, calculate the new dimensions after a 20% increase:
\[
\text{New width} = 24 \times 1.20 = 28.8 \text{ inches}
\]
\[
\text{New height} = 16 \times 1.20 = 19.2 \text{ inches}
\]

Now, calculate the new area:
\[
\text{New Area} = 28.8 \times 19.2 = 548.16 \text{ square inches}
\]

Finally, calculate the percentage increase in the area:
\[
\text{Percentage Increase} = \left( \frac{548.16 - 384}{384} \right) \times 100 \approx 17.04\%
\]

Final Answer: The final answer is approximately $17.04\%$. I hope it is correct.
