Problem:
The length of the diameter of this spherical ball is equal to the height of the box in which it is placed. The box is a cube and has an edge length of 30 cm. How many cubic centimeters of the box are not occupied by the solid sphere? Express your answer in terms of $\pi$. [asy]
draw(Circle((7.5,7.5),5));
draw((7.5,6.2)..(2.5,7.5)--(12.5,7.5)..cycle);
draw((7.5,8.8)..(2.5,7.5)--(12.5,7.5)..cycle,linetype("2 4"));
fill((2.6,7.4)--(2.6,7.6)--(12.4,7.6)--(12.4,7.4)--cycle,white);
dot((7.5,7.5));
draw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(0,10)--cycle);
draw((0,10)--(5,15)--(15,15)--(10,10));
draw((15,15)--(15,5)--(10,0));
draw((0,0)--(5,5)--(15,5),dashed); draw((5,5)--(5,15),dashed);
[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  The diameter of the sphere is equal to the height of the box, which is 30 cm. Therefore, the radius of the sphere is 15 cm. The volume of the sphere is given by the formula $\frac{4}{3}\pi r^3$, where $r$ is the radius. So, the volume of the sphere is

$$\frac{4}{3}\pi (15)^3 = \frac{4}{3}\pi (3375) = \frac{1000}{3}\pi.$$

The volume of the cube is given by the formula $a^3$, where $a$ is the edge length. So, the volume of the cube is

$$30^3 = 27000.$$

The volume of the box that is not occupied by the sphere is the volume of the cube minus the volume of the sphere:

$$27000 - \frac{1000}{3}\pi.$$

Therefore, the number of cubic centimeters of the box that are not occupied by the solid sphere is $\boxed{27000 - \frac{1000}{3}\pi}$.
====================

