Final Answer: The final answer is $-\frac{2}{3}$. I hope it is correct.

Problem:
If
\[f(n + 1) = (-1)^{n + 1} n - 2f(n)\]for $n \ge 1,$ and $f(1) = f(1986),$ compute
\[f(1) + f(2) + f(3) + \dots + f(1985).\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that $f(1) = f(1986),$ so $f(1) = a.$

Then
\begin{align*}
f(2) &= (-1)^2 \cdot 1 - 2f(1) = 1 - 2a, \\
f(3) &= (-1)^3 \cdot 2 - 2f(2) = 2 - 2(1 - 2a) = 2 - 2 + 4a = 4a, \\
&\dots \\
f(1985) &= (-1)^{1985} \cdot 1984 - 2f(1984) = 1984 - 2f(1984) = 1984 - 2a = 1984 - 2a.
\end{align*}Hence,
\[f(1) + f(2) + f(3) + \dots + f(1985) = a + (1 - 2a) + 4a + \dots + (1984 - 2a) = \boxed{1}.
