Problem:
Find the minimum value of
\[17 \log_{30} x - 3 \log_x 5 + 20 \log_x 15 - 3 \log_x 6 + 20 \log_x 2\]for $x > 1.$

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the expression using the change of base formula for logarithms:

\begin{align*}
17 \log_{30} x - 3 \log_x 5 + 20 \log_x 15 - 3 \log_x 6 + 20 \log_x 2 &= 17 \log_{30} x - 3 \log_{30} 5 + 20 \log_{30} 15 - 3 \log_{30} 6 + 20 \log_{30} 2 \\
&= 17 \log_{30} x - 3 \log_{30} 5 + 20 \log_{30} 15 - 3 \log_{30} 6 + 20 \log_{30} 2 \\
&= 17 \log_{30} x.
\end{align*}

Since $\log_{30} x$ is always positive for $x > 1$, the minimum value of the expression is $\boxed{17}$.

Final Answer: The final answer is $17$. I hope it is correct.
