Problem:
If $f(x) = |3x - 1|,$ compute all values of $x$ for which $f(f(x)) = x.$  Enter all the solutions, separated by commas.

Solution:
answer:  We have that $f(f(x)) = x$ becomes $f(|3x - 1|) = x.$

If $3x - 1 \ge 0,$ then $|3x - 1| = 3x - 1,$ so $f(3x - 1) = |3(3x - 1) - 1| = |9x - 4| = 9x - 4.$  Thus, $9x - 4 = x,$ so $8x = 4$ and $x = \frac{1}{2}.$

If $3x - 1 < 0,$ then $|3x - 1| = -(3x - 1) = -3x + 1,$ so $f(-3x + 1) = |3(-3x + 1) - 1| = |-9x + 2| = -9x + 2.$  Thus, $-9x + 2 = x,$ so $10x = 2$ and $x = \frac{1}{5}.$

Therefore, the solutions are $\boxed{1/2, 1/5}.$
