Problem:
Determine the value of the infinite sum
\[\sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the sum as
\[\sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \sum_{n = 17}^\infty \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \boxed{1}.\]
The answer is: 1
