Problem:
Determine the remainder when $$1+12+123+1234+12345+123456+1234567+12345678$$is divided by $5$.

Solution:
answer:  First, we find the remainder of each number when divided by $5$:

\begin{align*}
1 &\equiv 1 \pmod{5}, \\
12 &\equiv 2 \pmod{5}, \\
123 &\equiv 3 \pmod{5}, \\
1234 &\equiv 4 \pmod{5}, \\
12345 &\equiv 0 \pmod{5}, \\
123456 &\equiv 1 \pmod{5}, \\
1234567 &\equiv 2 \pmod{5}, \\
12345678 &\equiv 3 \pmod{5}.
\end{align*}

Next, we sum these remainders:

\begin{align*}
1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 0 + 1 + 2 + 3 &\equiv 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 0 + 1 + 2 + 3 \pmod{5} \\
&\equiv 16 \pmod{5}.
\end{align*}

Finally, the remainder when $16$ is divided by $5$ is $\boxed{1}$.
====================

