Problem:
On a Tuesday, a magician said, ``I made my wife disappear 31 days ago.'' What day of the week did he make her disappear?

Solution:
answer:  To determine the day of the week the magician made his wife disappear, we need to count backwards by 31 days from Tuesday.

1. Start with Tuesday.
2. Count backwards by 31 days.

Let's count the days:
- Tuesday (Day 1)
- Monday (Day 2)
- Sunday (Day 3)
- Saturday (Day 4)
- Friday (Day 5)
- Thursday (Day 6)
- Wednesday (Day 7)
- Tuesday (Day 8)
- Monday (Day 9)
- Sunday (Day 10)
- Saturday (Day 11)
- Friday (Day 12)
- Thursday (Day 13)
- Wednesday (Day 14)
- Tuesday (Day 15)
- Monday (Day 16)
- Sunday (Day 17)
- Saturday (Day 18)
- Friday (Day 19)
- Thursday (Day 20)
- Wednesday (Day 21)

So, the magician made his wife disappear on a \(\boxed{\text{Wednesday}}\).
