Problem:
What is the units digit when $7^{53}$ is multiplied out?

Solution:
answer:  To determine the units digit of \(7^{53}\), we can focus on the units digit of the base number, which is 7. We will observe the pattern in the units digits of the powers of 7:

\[
\begin{align*}
7^1 &= 7 \quad \text{(units digit is 7)} \\
7^2 &= 49 \quad \text{(units digit is 9)} \\
7^3 &= 343 \quad \text{(units digit is 3)} \\
7^4 &= 2401 \quad \text{(units digit is 1)} \\
\end{align*}
\]

We notice that the units digits repeat every 4 powers: 7, 9, 3, 1. To find the units digit of \(7^{53}\), we need to determine the position of 53 in the repeating cycle. Since \(53 \mod 4 = 1\), \(7^{53}\) will have the same units digit as \(7^1\), which is 7.

Therefore, the units digit of \(7^{53}\) is \boxed{7}.
