Problem:
The exam grades of a pre-algebra class were arranged in a stem and leaf plot as illustrated. What is the arithmetic mean of the median and the mode of the given data?

\begin{tabular}{ c | c c c ccc c c c}
4&1&&&&&&&&\\
5&2&&&&&&&&\\
6&7&8&8&&&&&&\\
7&1&1&2&3&3&3&5&6&8\\
8&0&4&4&6&6&6&6&8&\\
9&1&3&5&5&7&&&&\\
\end{tabular}

Solution:
answer:  First, we need to find the median and the mode of the data.

The median is the middle value when the data is arranged in ascending order. From the stem and leaf plot, we can arrange the data as follows:

41, 52, 67, 68, 68, 71, 71, 72, 73, 73, 75, 76, 78, 80, 84, 84, 86, 86, 86, 88, 91, 93, 95, 95, 97

The median is the 11th value, which is 73.

The mode is the value that appears most frequently in the data. From the stem and leaf plot, we can see that 73 appears 3 times, which is more frequent than any other value.

Now, we find the arithmetic mean of the median and the mode:

$$\frac{73 + 73}{2} = \frac{146}{2} = \boxed{73}$$
