Problem:
A 420-page book contains an average of 600 words per page, and Roslyn reads the book at the rate of 360 words per minute. How many hours did it take her to read the book? Express your answer as a mixed number.

Solution:
answer:  First, we need to determine the total number of words in the book. The book has 420 pages and contains an average of 600 words per page:

\[
420 \text{ pages} \times 600 \text{ words/page} = 252,000 \text{ words}
\]

Next, we need to find out how many minutes it took Roslyn to read the book. She reads at a rate of 360 words per minute:

\[
\frac{252,000 \text{ words}}{360 \text{ words/minute}} = 700 \text{ minutes}
\]

Finally, we convert the total minutes into hours:

\[
\frac{700 \text{ minutes}}{60 \text{ minutes/hour}} = 11.67 \text{ hours}
\]

To express 11.67 as a mixed number, we note:

\[
11.67 = 11 \frac{2}{3}
\]

\(\boxed{11 \frac{2}{3}}\)
