Problem:
The Asian elephant has an average gestation period of 609 days. How many weeks is this gestation period?

Solution:
answer:  To convert the gestation period from days to weeks, we need to divide the number of days by 7, since there are 7 days in a week.

\[
609 \text{ days} \div 7 \text{ days/week} = 87 \text{ weeks}
\]

Therefore, the gestation period of the Asian elephant is \boxed{87} weeks.
